# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  SECRETS — every credential the API reads, in one place
#
#  Loaded by server/src/config.ts, after server/.env. Kept separate from .env on
#  purpose: .env holds settings (ports, model names, timeouts, cron expressions)
#  that are worth reading, diffing and sharing, while this file holds the values
#  that must never be shared. Splitting them means you can hand someone your
#  configuration without handing them your keys.
#
#  ── PRECEDENCE ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  server/.env is read FIRST and WINS. dotenv never overwrites a variable that
#  is already set, so a key present in both files resolves to .env. Do not
#  duplicate a key across the two — keep every credential here and nowhere else.
#  The boot summary prints which files it read: `env files   .env → secrets.env`.
#
#  ── AFTER EDITING, RESTART THE API ────────────────────────────────────────
#  Values are read lazily at call time, but dotenv loads this file once at
#  import. A running process will not notice a new key until it restarts.
#      npm run dev:server        (or touch any file under server/src/)
#
#  ── NOTHING HERE IS REQUIRED ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Every key may be left blank. The product runs with all of them empty; each
#  blank switches a real degraded path and labels itself in the UI. A blank key
#  never produces invented data — it produces a stated absence.
#
#  ── THIS FILE IS GITIGNORED. NEVER COMMIT IT. ─────────────────────────────
#  server/secrets.env is gitignored; this file is not. Keep every value blank here.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ═══ SCRAPING ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Apify reads the four platform lanes — LinkedIn, Instagram, X, Facebook — and
# returns REAL reaction, comment and repost counts.
#
# BLANK ⇒ those lanes fall back to crawl4ai, which reads what a search engine
# indexed and therefore states no engagement at all. Three of the four
# components of `trend_score` are engagement maths, so they are set aside and
# every keyword is scored on volume alone, with the caveat printed on the score.
# The lane still answers; it answers with less.
#
# Token: Apify console → Settings → API & Integrations → Personal API tokens.
# Sent as an Authorization: Bearer header, never in a query string.
APIFY_API_TOKEN=


# ═══ RESEARCH ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Parallel Web Systems performs the deep-research synthesis behind the
# Knowledge Base.
#
# BLANK ⇒ the Knowledge Agent reads the open web with crawl4ai instead, and the
# reason is recorded on every entry it writes. There is no bundled research
# corpus: an uncited claim never enters the Knowledge Base, so nothing is
# substituted when neither source answers.
PARALLEL_API_KEY=


# ═══ HOSTED MODELS · Google Cloud ══════════════════════════════════════════
# Gemini writes captions and calendar copy; Imagen paints creative backgrounds.
# Either an API key (AI Studio) or a service account is enough.
#
# BLANK ⇒ text falls to whichever local model is configured in .env
# (TEXT_MODEL_PROVIDER / OLLAMA_*), and then to the deterministic template
# writer. Images fall to the local brand SVG renderer. Both stamp the reason on
# the card they produced.
GCP_API_KEY=

# Vertex instead of the public API. Naming a project switches the endpoints.
GCP_SERVICE_ACCOUNT_JSON=


# ═══ OPTIONAL IMAGE RENDERER ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
# A secondary hosted renderer. Blank ⇒ not offered in the model menu at all.
Z_IMAGE_API_KEY=


# ═══ PLATFORM PUBLISHING ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DELIBERATELY EMPTY, AND NOT YET WIRED.
#
# No publishing credentials exist in the codebase. `liveAdapter` in
# server/src/agents/publishing/handlers.ts implements the adapter interface and
# refuses with a specific message; PUBLISH_MODE=live therefore refuses too, and
# demo mode simulates every call and stamps `demo` permanently on the receipt.
#
# The keys below are listed so the shape is known, NOT because setting them does
# anything today. Publishing needs the OAuth flow, an encrypted token store and
# the platform adapters built first — filling these in will not make a post go
# out, and the product will keep telling you so rather than pretending.
#
# LINKEDIN_CLIENT_ID=
# LINKEDIN_CLIENT_SECRET=
# INSTAGRAM_APP_ID=
# INSTAGRAM_APP_SECRET=
